WEBVTT

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:04.330
When sales weaken, who still gets funded
and for how much?

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:08.410
I tested 2,500 simulated businesses

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.420
with advances repaid from daily sales.

00:00:11.853 --> 00:00:16.133
I launched Module 1
from PowerShell on AWS.

00:00:16.653 --> 00:00:19.813
It verified the inputs
and returned a checkpoint.

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:23.390
Module 2 picked up that checkpoint
the next day

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:27.340
and followed each funded account
for 120 days.

00:00:27.738 --> 00:00:30.418
Together, 5,000 decisions

00:00:30.498 --> 00:00:33.848
took 2 hours and 24 minutes
of computation.

00:00:34.375 --> 00:00:39.525
In Tableau, 329 businesses
receive funding in Baseline.

00:00:40.375 --> 00:00:44.405
100 of them also receive funding
under Recession Energy.

00:00:44.915 --> 00:00:47.085
Of the other 229,

00:00:47.385 --> 00:00:52.165
21 went to review
and 208 were declined.

00:00:52.605 --> 00:00:59.135
Those businesses explain over 99%
of a $3.35 million gap.

00:00:59.695 --> 00:01:02.515
Four smaller offers explain the rest.

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:05.950
Take merchant 002191.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:09.430
Power BI shows this online business

00:01:09.470 --> 00:01:15.100
received the full $22,800
it requested for expansion.

00:01:15.603 --> 00:01:18.933
Under stress, it received $9,200

00:01:19.453 --> 00:01:21.663
at the same share of daily sales.

00:01:22.103 --> 00:01:26.953
The stress model first selected $18,200.

00:01:27.473 --> 00:01:32.973
The final policy ruled it out because
its share of sales fell below Baseline.

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:36.770
The smaller advance paid off on day 37,

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:39.360
before the shock reached collections.

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:43.180
The larger Baseline advance took 91 days.

00:01:43.532 --> 00:01:46.392
Could collecting a smaller share
of daily sales

00:01:46.432 --> 00:01:48.682
keep more financing within reach?

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:53.532
I’d test whether those larger advances
still repay.

